Make Bindings::emptyBindings thread_local instead of a plain global static.

nix::EvalMemory::allocBindings (src/libexpr/attr-set.cc) returns this one
shared singleton for every zero-capacity Bindings request across the whole
process, as a micro-optimization to avoid allocating for `{}` literals. But
nix::ExprAttrs::eval (src/libexpr/eval.cc) unconditionally writes
`bindings.bindings->pos = pos` on whatever Bindings it gets back -- for the
capacity==0 case that's an unsynchronized write to the shared global from
every thread that evaluates an empty attribute set, which is extremely
common in real Nix expressions. Confirmed via ThreadSanitizer against
nanopynix's concurrent-EvalState test suite: this is by far the dominant
race (1373 of 1376 total TSAN reports in one run all point at this single
line), and directly contradicts attr-set.hh's own doc comment on
emptyBindings ("This object must never be modified.").

thread_local gives each thread its own private empty-Bindings instance,
preserving the original allocation-avoidance optimization within a thread
while eliminating the cross-thread sharing that causes the race.

diff -ruN a/src/libexpr/attr-set.cc b/src/libexpr/attr-set.cc
--- a/src/libexpr/attr-set.cc	2026-07-18 20:24:48.025253282 +0200
+++ b/src/libexpr/attr-set.cc	2026-07-18 20:24:48.033043934 +0200
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 namespace nix {
 
-Bindings Bindings::emptyBindings;
+thread_local Bindings Bindings::emptyBindings;
 
 /* Allocate a new array of attributes for an attribute set with a specific
    capacity. The space is implicitly reserved after the Bindings
diff -ruN a/src/libexpr/include/nix/expr/attr-set.hh b/src/libexpr/include/nix/expr/attr-set.hh
--- a/src/libexpr/include/nix/expr/attr-set.hh	2026-07-18 20:24:48.023253271 +0200
+++ b/src/libexpr/include/nix/expr/attr-set.hh	2026-07-18 20:24:48.030253310 +0200
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@
      * An instance of bindings objects with 0 attributes.
      * This object must never be modified.
      */
-    static Bindings emptyBindings;
+    static thread_local Bindings emptyBindings;
 
 private:
     /**
